# MASTER PROMPT — SIGNBRIDGE AI

## AI-Powered Indian Sign Language Recognition and Accessible Communication Platform

Act as a senior full-stack developer, computer vision engineer, machine learning engineer, accessibility specialist, and UI/UX designer.

Build a complete, functional, production-structured MVP named **SignBridge AI**.

Do not create only a landing page, UI mockup, static dashboard, or nonfunctional prototype. Build a working application with real webcam access, hand landmark detection, a pluggable ISL recognition pipeline, text output, speech output, dataset management, and model evaluation tools.

The application must run in a modern desktop browser and be designed primarily for laptop and PC webcam use.

==================================================

1. PROJECT VISION
   ==================================================

Project name: SignBridge AI

Full title:
AI-Powered Indian Sign Language Recognition and Accessible Communication System for Inclusive Interaction.

Primary objective:

Develop an accessible computer vision application that recognizes selected Indian Sign Language (ISL) signs through a webcam, converts recognized signs into readable text, and speaks the resulting messages aloud.

The application is intended to support communication between:

1. Deaf or hard-of-hearing sign-language users.
2. Blind or visually impaired people who depend on spoken information.
3. People who do not understand sign language but need to communicate with sign-language users.

Example workflow:

A deaf person performs a verified ISL sign in front of a webcam.

The application detects the hand landmarks.

The recognition engine predicts the corresponding trained sign label.

The application maps that label to its verified English or Tamil message.

The message appears on the screen.

Text-to-speech announces the message.

Example output:
Recognized message: "I need water."

Spoken output:
"I need water."

This is an illustrative example, not a claim that a particular hand pose necessarily means that phrase in ISL.

Important limitation:
ISL is a natural language, not simply a collection of universal hand poses. Begin with a clearly defined vocabulary of verified signs. Do not claim complete ISL translation or production-level accuracy without sufficient training data and independent evaluation.

