5. WEBCAM AND HAND LANDMARK DETECTION
=====================================

Implement real webcam access.

Requirements:

* Request permission only after the user presses Start Camera.
* Use getUserMedia().
* Stop all media tracks when the camera is stopped.
* Clean up camera streams when the component unmounts.
* Handle permission denial.
* Handle no available camera.
* Handle camera already in use.
* Handle unsupported browsers.
* Avoid starting multiple camera streams accidentally.

Use MediaPipe Hand Landmarker or Gesture Recognizer.

Where Hand Landmarker is used:

* Detect up to two hands when supported by the configuration.
* Extract the 21 landmarks for each detected hand.
* Display landmarks and connections on a canvas overlay.
* Use requestAnimationFrame or a suitable real-time frame processing strategy.
* Avoid processing frames unnecessarily.
* Keep the interface responsive.

Show accurate status messages:

* Camera not started.
* Waiting for permission.
* Camera active.
* No hand detected.
* Hand detected.
* Recognition model unavailable.
* Ready for recognition.
* Prediction uncertain.

Do not interpret hand detection as proof that a sign has been understood.

