8. TRAINING AND EVALUATION
==========================

Create a separate model evaluation workflow.

Required metrics:

* Accuracy.
* Precision.
* Recall.
* F1-score.
* Per-class performance.
* Confusion matrix.
* Test sample count.
* Number of classes.
* Model version.
* Dataset source.

Use signer-independent or session-independent evaluation wherever possible.

Do not randomly split adjacent frames from the same video into training and test sets. This can cause data leakage and misleadingly high scores.

UNKNOWN GESTURE HANDLING

Implement:

* A configurable confidence threshold.
* Prediction smoothing.
* A minimum stability period.
* Duplicate announcement prevention.
* An explicit uncertain state.
* A reset mechanism after each accepted sign.

Important:
A classifier's confidence value is not automatically a calibrated probability.

Do not announce low-confidence predictions as certain messages.

For emergency-related messages, make uncertainty particularly clear. Do not advertise the MVP as a reliable emergency communication device.

